== 3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD, with the partition the body induces (RECORDED: the greps) ==
  RECORDED `grep -n warned_unimpl' fix568b (every reader and writer of the latch field):
      59:     uint64_t    warned_unimpl;
      62: /*  #568: a warned_unimpl narrower than VME2_MISC >> 2 + 1 bits would
      67:     8 * sizeof(((struct vme_data *)0)->warned_unimpl) ? 1 : -1];
     192:         if (!(d->warned_unimpl & (1ULL << (relative_addr >> 2)))) {
     193:             d->warned_unimpl |= 1ULL << (relative_addr >> 2);
  RECORDED `grep -n memset' fix568b:
      57:         VME2_MISC (0x8c >> 2 == 35).  Zeroed by DEVINIT's memset, so every
     235:     memset(d, 0, sizeof(struct vme_data));
  WRITERS of warned_unimpl: the arm's `|=' and DEVINIT's memset ONLY -- no state where guard field and body field
  disagree is buildable within one instance (one vme device per process: NOT CLAIMED).
  Partitions the arm's body induces, per lvalue:
    writeflag      tested `== MEM_WRITE' -> {READ, WRITE} -- EXHAUSTED (both rowed at every label: the ann pair)
    latch bit      tested by the guard -> {clear, set} -- EXHAUSTED (pass 1 clear, pass 2 set)
    label (26)     each a dispatch label whose value flows into the latch index -> a FLOOR AXIS (26 x 2 x 2 = 104
                   cells, the ann pair)
    len            NOT tested by the fixed body (printed only) -- SAMPLED: 1, 2, 4, 8 by the non-word rows (one
                   register per width) and the width rows at 0x28 / 0x08; the latch-hold across widths now rowed
                   (`p2 nw rd 2', `p2 nw wr 2')
    idata          NOT tested by the fixed body (printed in the write form); the operand swap M_IDATA makes the
                   direction test read idata's zero-ness -> {0, non-0}: the 0 cell at a first access is rowed by
                   `p2 zero wr' (one width, len 4), the non-0 cell by every other store -- DEPENDS-ON clause (2)
    odata          NOT tested (printed in the read form; always 0 today: M_ODATA0 / M_SERVED0 equivalent)
  `default:': no predicate of its own (the switch's fallthrough); the body tests writeflag (which debug())
  -> {READ, WRITE} and nothing else.  The refusal-narrowing mutants each condition `return 0' on a lvalue the
  body reads: len (M_FLTLEN), writeflag (M_FLTWR), len x lane (M_LANE0H, M_LANE0B) -- rowed by `p1 widths' (8
  accesses: len 1, 2 and 8, lanes 0-3, both directions) and the stepped fault rows (len 4).

